# Suppression rules for examples/multiple_leaks.cpp.
#
# Used by the integration test, and a working example of the format. Each rule
# is `<scope>:<glob>`; see docs/USAGE.md for the full description.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. A malformed line is a hard
# error rather than a warning: a typo here silently changes what the tool
# reports, and finding that out from a green CI run is worse than a startup
# failure.

# leakSmall() allocates 100 blocks we have decided not to fix. `*` is needed at
# both ends because the demangled name carries the anonymous namespace and the
# parameter list: "(anonymous namespace)::leakSmall()".
function:*leakSmall*

# The other two sites (leakMedium, leakOne) are deliberately NOT suppressed --
# the test asserts they still appear, because a suppression file that quietly
# covers more than it names is the failure mode that matters here.
